<title>RUSSIA: Russia's VSM sets terms for next bond.</title>
<headline>Russia's VSM sets terms for next bond.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's RAO Vysokoskorostnye Magistrali (VSM or High-Speed Railways) set terms for its third bond issue to be auctioned on March 20 on the Moscow Interbank Currency Exchange, the exchange said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number		     RU22VSM0330</p>
<p>    Issue volume			150 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Tenor				 365 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			  March 20, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date		     March 20, 1998</p>
<p>    Coupon dates			June 20, 1997</p>
<p>					    September 20, 1997</p>
<p>					    December 20, 1997</p>
<p>					    March 20, 1998</p>
<p>    First coupon rate		 32.74 pct (8,251 rbls)</p>
<p>--Anna Smirnova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
